# Template only — NOT loaded by firebase-tools, which looks for `.env`, `.env.<projectId>` and
# `.env.<alias>`. Copy the block below to the real filename before a prod functions deploy.
#
# ⚠️ PROD IS NOT CONFIGURED AND THE FILE IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT FROM THIS REPO. Setting it is
# Nick's, alongside the deploy it enables — see CLAUDE.md, "Functions — the database is named".
# Until it exists, every function REFUSES TO START on prod rather than writing to a database that
# is not there. That is the intended state, not an outage to be patched around.
#
# ---- functions/.env.gen-lang-client-0801391782 ----
# FIRESTORE_DATABASE_ID=ai-studio-ae82196c-c59e-40b9-b209-9fb02f67ade6
# WAITLIST_FROM="Nick at QueryHawk <nick@queryhawk.net>"
# WAITLIST_REPLY_TO=nick@queryhawk.net
# WAITLIST_CONTACT_EMAIL=hello@queryhawk.net
# WAITLIST_PUBLIC_URL=https://queryhawk.net
# ---------------------------------------------------
#
# ⚠️ THE MAIL KEYS ARE queryhawk.net, AND NOTHING MAY NAME scriptally.ink. That domain was deleted
# from Resend on 17 Oct, so a FROM on it is rejected. WAITLIST_FROM is quoted because the display
# name has spaces and angle brackets; "at", not "@", in the name (see emailConfig.ts).
#
# Verified 26 Aug with `firebase firestore:databases:list`:
#   gen-lang-client-0801391782  →  ai-studio-ae82196c-…   ONLY. There is no (default).
#   scriptally-dev              →  (default)              ONLY.

# ══════════════ functions/.env — UNTRACKED, and now optional ══════════════
#
# firebase-tools loads `.env` first, then `.env.<projectId>`, then `.env.<alias>`, so a value in the
# per-project file WINS over the same key in the bare `.env`. Anything that should not be published
# goes in the bare `.env`, which .gitignore excludes — THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC.
#
# Until 17 Oct this file carried a personal WAITLIST_REPLY_TO and WAITLIST_CONTACT_EMAIL, because
# forwarding on the old domain did not deliver. The queryhawk.net mailbox does, and both values are
# now stated in each per-project file, which overrides them here.
#
# ⚠️ WAITLIST_CONTACT_EMAIL IS THE ADDRESS EACH EMAIL PRINTS IN ITS BODY, and it is separate from
# the reply-to for a reason: a reader cannot SEE a Reply-To header, so a dead one fails invisibly,
# whereas a printed address that bounces is a promise broken in the text of the email. Unset it
# falls back to SUPPORT_EMAIL (hello@queryhawk.net).
#
# Unset WAITLIST_REPLY_TO is survivable: the transport falls back to the from-address and logs a
# warning. It never throws — a missing reply route must not stop a confirmation going out.
